        "id": 1042276
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-10T20:42:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is Android specific.  Android excludes the 32-bit build on device.  Since the fuse crate then doesn\u0027t have the 32-bit variant, we need this rule to also not generate the 32-bit variant (which we won\u0027t need anyway).\n\nFor reference, here is the rule that all crates under crosvm uses, which only enable necessary build selectively.\n\nhttps://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:external/crosvm/Android.bp;l\u003d18-29?q\u003dcrosvm%2FAndroid.bp",
      "parentUuid": "d87ca325_41e8b722",
      "revId": "6ddab6e3ef4f5fc08b84b5344bbbee5f7e348841",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77b3aea4_be5ed148",
        "filename": "authfs/src/fusefs.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 52,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074798
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-12-10T07:12:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The default hash function used by HashMap is siphash, which is designed to prevent hash collision attacks and not for performance.  So if you trust the source of the keys then you may want to change the hash function to something like fnv (using the fnv crate).\n\n\nAdditionally, since the keys are already integers in this case I suspect that a BTreeMap will likely outperform even a fnv HashMap here unless you are storing thousands of entries.",
      "revId": "6ddab6e3ef4f5fc08b84b5344bbbee5f7e348841",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5a187ec5_47717ba7",
        "filename": "authfs/src/fusefs.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
